    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d89">

                <pb facs="0167" n="101" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg101"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/4619: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Personal Representative of the President</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-15T19:00:00-05:00">January 15, 1934—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>24. My telegram No. 22, January 15, 2 p.m. After much delay today Grau finally
                    turned over the office of Provisional President to Hevia at 5 p.m., and
                    proceeded to his private house. (Hevia will take oath of office tomorrow.) I was
                    asked to make a personal visit on Grau at once for protection reasons and have
                    done so (having in mind the attitude of the opposition parties to him of
                    course).</p>
                <p>A mob around the Palace was dispersed by the troops shortly after Grau left, with
                    1 killed and 14 wounded.</p>
                <p>There is much nervousness in the city and possible danger of conflict between
                    Batista’s forces and those of the Cuban factions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
